# Command Center lists, nodes, and badges

This is mandatory on every Command Center page. It keeps getting reverted. Do not ship a page that breaks it, and do not restore the old pill look.

## Lists scroll

Every list (memory, nodes, files, search, unresolved, rules, skills, logging, prices, savings, settings tables) scrolls inside its own panel.

- The list is `overflow-y: auto` with `min-height: 0`.
- A parent with `overflow: hidden` must not clip the list. The list itself is the scroll container.
- Headers and filters stay put. The rows move.

## Active row

The selected list row has both a highlight and a border. A background fill alone is not enough.

- Highlight: `color-mix` of the theme accent over the panel.
- Border: 1px `var(--accent-text)`, including an inset outline so the row reads as selected on every list.
- Hover only changes the background. The border belongs to the selected row.

## Active nodes

The selected graph node (memory timeline, and the same marker anywhere else) is not a flat filled circle.

- A ring of tiny dots (about 1px) orbits the node counter-clockwise.
- The center is a filled dot that breathes (soft scale and opacity pulse).
- Idle nodes stay hollow rings.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`: show the filled center, no orbit and no pulse.

## Badges

Every badge is a square outline chip: height 16px, padding 0 6px, **`border-radius: 0`**. Straight corners.

Inside the calm lists (`.calm-list`, `.memory-vault-list`: Memory, Rules, Skills, Logging) badges are smaller and quieter: height 14px, padding 0 4px, 10px text, a hairline border (1px, 0.5px on 2x screens) in the theme color mixed to about 40%. Timeline dots there are 12px and sit at least 12px from the row's left edge; no inset color stripe on the row.

The old requirement that pills use rounded corners (`border-radius: 999px` or `8px`) is revoked. Do not put `border-radius: 999px` back on `.page-item-badge`, `.policy-pack-badge`, `.ax-project-badge`, `.mcp-q-strip-badge`, `.status-quality-badge`, `.settings-embed-badge`, `.lsp-server-badge`, `.settings-share-badge`, or any other badge class. The macOS theme must not round them either.

Fill is transparent. Text is `#cccccc` at 11px. The border and the icon use the active theme: `var(--accent-text)` by default, `var(--warn)` for a warning, `var(--danger)` for an error, `var(--ok)` for ok. Do not hardcode `#3794ff`, `#e07070`, `#e0b341`, or `#3ee4b2` on a badge.

Every badge, including a `+N` count and a badge that would otherwise be text-only, starts with a 12px codicon (`class="badge-icon"`, `aria-hidden`). If a callsite forgets the element, the badge CSS `::before` fallback still paints a glyph. The icon uses the border hue. The text stays `#cccccc`.

| Badge | Icon |
|---|---|
| Git branch, git memory, extra `+N` | `git-branch` |
| Tag | `tag` |
| Language or symbol kind | `symbol-misc` |
| Exported / pub | `eye` |
| Critical / error / quality count | `error` |
| Warning | `warning` |
| Info / confidence | `info` |
| Project or project database | `repo` |
| Global database | `globe` |
| Company | `organization` |
| Workspace | `window` |
| Private user | `person` |
| Private project | `lock` |
| Memory kind | kind icon (`note`, `law`, `bug`, `symbol-structure`, `checklist`, `git-commit`) |
| Live / running | `play` |
| Inbound trace | `arrow-down` |
| Outbound trace | `arrow-up` |
| Search / query | `search` |

Do not use a filled chip, a rounded pill, colored badge text, or a badge with no icon. Do not give one page its own badge shape.

